@@ -0,0 +1,25 @@
+---
+id: dl-008-the-patch-given-to-applymergepatch-must-be-a-json-value-checked-deeply-before-any-merge-runs
+type: decision-log
+title: "The patch given to applyMergePatch must be a JSON value, checked deeply before any merge runs"
+status: pending
+format: 1
+---
+
+## Context
+
+RFC 7386 defines a merge patch as a JSON document. A patch containing `undefined`, `NaN`, `Infinity`,
+functions, `Date` objects or sparse arrays is not JSON, and would be copied into the result. dl-005 makes
+the same requirement for the `value` of a JSON Patch operation, checked before any operation runs.
+
+## Decision
+
+`applyMergePatch` checks the whole `patch` deeply, with the same JSON-value test as dl-005, before it
+merges anything. A patch that is not a JSON value throws. The `target` is not checked, as `applyPatch`
+does not check its document; the result is only as valid as the target the caller supplies.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- An invalid patch is rejected before any part of it is applied, and no result is returned.
+- Validating the patch costs a walk over it, before the merge walk.
+- Callers building patches in code must pass JSON values; `undefined` means no member and is not a value.
